✋ ConstraintError: cannot tell which machine this is — no platform probe answered

   asked, in order (each name is grove_env_probe_<name>):
     house            (a root-owned election in /etc/grove/house.d names this login) → no
     aws_ec2          (dmi vendor · systemd-detect-virt · cloud-init · xen uuid)   → no
     hetzner_hetzbot  (the platform declaration == hetzner.hetzbot)                → no
     desktop          (WAYLAND_DISPLAY · DISPLAY · XDG_SESSION_TYPE, not over ssh) → no
     aws_ec2_imds     (169.254.169.254, capped at 1s)                              → no

   why this is an error and not a guess:
     a guess here would be 'local@unix', which every interactive step
     reads as 'a human is at a keyboard'. on a headless box that opens
     a prompt nobody can answer. so it refuses instead.

   fix — name the box yourself:
     GROVE_ENV_SERVER=local@unix            grove.provision   # a laptop
     GROVE_ENV_SERVER=house@unix            grove.provision   # a house grove seat
     GROVE_ENV_SERVER=cloud@aws.ec2         grove.provision   # an ec2 grove
     GROVE_ENV_SERVER=cloud@hetzner.hetzbot grove.provision   # a hetzner grove

   on a hetzner grove, the durable fix is its bootstrap: it writes one
   line, 'hetzner.hetzbot', into the platform declaration:
     <fixture>/platform
   infra's hetzner bootstrap owns that write — ask 3 of this repo's
     .behavior/v2026_10_25.feat-tailscale-on-every-machine/handoff.infra.grove-tailnet-join.md
   the override above serves one run until that file lands.
   on your laptop over ssh: the desktop rung declines an ssh seat, so
   name it local@unix, or run at the laptop's own keyboard.

   and if this box is one we own, the probe is what is wrong, not the box.
   each probe above is one command; run them by hand and read which lies.
